  "title": "Pollen refills got smaller and more frequent",
  "summary": "Pollen became easier to manage, image workflows gained useful controls, and the community catalog grew while the underlying routes got a careful tune-up.\n\nSpore and Seed changed to hourly refills that top balances up to a tier’s cap rather than resetting them. Accounts now report the next refill time where applicable, and balance checks account for estimated request costs. Fixes to ElevenMusic MP3 estimates and anomalous usage estimates address false 402 responses; model pricing averages also stopped counting successful zero-price requests.\n\nPlay added drag-and-drop and click-to-browse reference images with upload feedback. Flux Klein 4B edits can use up to four references instead of only the first. Pruna image edits now receive image URLs in the form they accept, Vertex AI passes through image-edit seeds and maps supported 512×512 Nano Banana requests to 1K, and Nano Banana moved to the stable gemini-2.5-flash-image model.\n\nNew additions span interactive stories, writing tools, games, image apps, desktop assistants, hardware experiments, and developer examples. Among them are House Painter for exterior color previews, NEURGenerator for ESP32-S3 hardware, a Claude Code plugin, and an app combining images, music, and text.\n\nThe Models page switched from expanding sections to tabs and responsive cards, with more complete per-Pollen estimates. Model Monitor now includes audio and video, separates models by endpoint, and makes degraded or off states clearer. A Qwen3.5 397B route was added, then removed from the registry after provider requests failed.",
